WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:36.860
[Music]

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:40.460
[Dr. Spock:] We show our love for our children in different ways.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:42.980
We give them good things to eat.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.520
We protect them from the cold or the heat.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:50.300
We teach them how to get along with each other.

00:00:51.520 --> 00:00:54.520
We comfort them when they're hurt.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:59.300
When they're sick, we do our best to get them well again.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:05.260
Even more important in the long run are the things we do to keep them healthy.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:09.500
That's why I feel unhappy about Jim here.

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:11.320
Look in his mouth.

00:01:11.320 --> 00:01:14.400
Can you see the missing and decayed teeth?

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.140
And he is just 14 years old.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:22.900
This bothers me because two-thirds of this decay could and really should have been prevented.

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:23.880
Think of it.

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:30.880
In many of our communities, we let our children have 65 percent more cavities, fillings, extractions,

00:01:30.880 --> 00:01:34.640
and toothaches than they need to suffer.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:37.660
Sixty-five percent.

00:01:37.660 --> 00:01:42.580
If parents knew they were letting their children have toothaches, cavities, and extractions,

00:01:42.580 --> 00:01:43.940
it would shock them.

00:01:43.940 --> 00:01:45.580
But it's true.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.160
Most decay can be prevented.

00:01:48.160 --> 00:01:52.920
Tooth decay is the most prevalent of all diseases in the United States.

00:01:52.920 --> 00:02:00.480
It begins just a few years after the appearance of the baby teeth and continues right through adulthood.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.780
The toll in lost teeth is high.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:06.840
It can spoil appearances, too.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:10.680
It can lead to abscesses and other diseases.

00:02:12.600 --> 00:02:17.060
Here's Fred, sixteen years old and a fine, healthy boy.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:20.880
But look at his teeth.

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.640
He's already lost several and has ten more with cavities.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.580
Here's the mouth of the average 40-year-old.

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.980
Half his teeth are gone.

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:35.140
So we can anticipate, without much pleasure,

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:40.760
that on the average, our youngsters will have lost half their teeth when they reach forty.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:47.940
You might think this is unusual, but 22 million Americans have no teeth at all.

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:52.680
More than a million of them are under 34.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:57.900
One child in ten has some form of malocclusion or crooked teeth.

00:02:58.700 --> 00:03:03.820
Bad cases like this one are a real social and psychological handicap.

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:07.460
Treatment means braces and dental bills.

00:03:07.460 --> 00:03:09.160
So that's the picture.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:17.500
Decay, pain, infection, facial disfigurement, 22 million people without teeth.

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:26.680
But, in about a thousand communities, almost everyone has attractive teeth,

00:03:26.690 --> 00:03:32.230
and there are many fewer cavities, less malocclusion, fewer dentures.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:33.660
Why?

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:38.050
The right amount of fluoride is present in their water supplies.

00:03:38.050 --> 00:03:40.730
It's always been there, naturally.

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:46.080
Here they are: a thousand towns where nature has provided the right amount of fluoride.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.920
Here's Patricia, who lives in one of those communities.

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:53.760
She's 16 and has been drinking fluoridated water since she was a baby.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:58.080
She has all her teeth and just three cavities.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:03.480
Compare that with the mouth of a 16-year-old from a non-fluoride town:

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:07.560
several teeth gone and as many as ten with cavities.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:09.140
This is Mr. Conway.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:11.460
He lives in a fluoride town.

00:04:11.460 --> 00:04:16.840
He's 40 years old and started drinking naturally fluoridated water when he was a baby.

00:04:17.220 --> 00:04:21.620
He's lost only three teeth and has seven fillings.

00:04:21.620 --> 00:04:26.180
Incidentally, all these facts about teeth are based on research findings.

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:27.400
They're not guesses,

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:34.220
but actual averages obtained by examining thousands of people in fluoride and non-fluoride towns.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:42.080
As you look at our map again, you should think of the adverse claims you have heard about fluoridation.

00:04:42.080 --> 00:04:47.860
That it's dangerous, causes heart disease, cancer, diabetes, and other diseases.

00:04:47.860 --> 00:04:51.580
If the unfavorable things you hear about fluoridation were true,

00:04:51.580 --> 00:04:54.740
no one in his right mind would live in these places.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:04:57.420
They'd be ghost towns.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:06.160
Think about all these towns, the millions of people in them, the thousands of physicians serving them.

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:10.160
Of course, practically all drinking water contains some fluoride.

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:14.400
So all our lives, most of us have been drinking water with a little fluoride in it.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:19.360
We also get a little fluoride in the food we eat.

00:05:19.360 --> 00:05:22.980
There's really no such thing as a fluoride-free diet.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:27.700
Chicken has 1.4 parts per million of fluoride.

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:30.220
Spinach, 1 part per million.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:32.520
Corn, 1 part per million.

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:35.220
Butter, 1.5.

00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:37.760
Milk, about 0.1.

00:05:37.760 --> 00:05:41.680
Bread, 1.0.

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:46.080
In fact, a diet lacking in fluoride would be an inadequate diet.

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:48.760
Whether the fluoride is added in by nature

00:05:48.760 --> 00:05:56.220
or by engineers in precise amounts under controlled conditions, the fluoride is always the same.

00:05:56.220 --> 00:05:59.900
It's released in the water and absorbed by the blood.

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:05.080
Some is stored in the teeth and bones, and the rest is excreted from the body.

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:10.760
You'll find controlled fluoridation in more than 2,600 communities.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:13.940
Some are little places, just a few hundred people.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:19.480
Others are cities like San Francisco, Denver, Baltimore,

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:25.640
Chicago, Philadelphia, Cleveland, Milwaukee, and Miami.

00:06:30.300 --> 00:06:33.460
You'll find controlled fluoridation in Washington,

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:38.180
where Congress appropriated funds for adding fluoride to the city's water.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:42.320
So the President's family drinks fluoridated water.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:47.420
In fact, one out of every three people in the United States who use a public water supply

00:06:47.420 --> 00:06:50.980
drinks water with a controlled fluoride content.

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:58.120
All the major scientific and professional groups concerned with health have long supported fluoridation.

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:01.700
Opponents of fluoridation have asserted that all sorts of things

00:07:01.700 --> 00:07:05.080
would happen when communities decided to fluoridate,

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:09.820
but in not a single instance have their predictions materialized.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:14.120
Some opponents have claimed fluoridation is unconstitutional.

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:20.880
This is really like saying that vaccination or the chlorination of the water supply are unconstitutional.

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:25.880
Actually, the courts say that fluoridation is constitutional.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:30.020
Let's take a look at what controlled fluoridation actually has done.

00:07:30.020 --> 00:07:32.440
Here's Grand Rapids, Michigan.

00:07:32.450 --> 00:07:36.470
In 1945, the fluoride content of the water was adjusted

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:41.010
to the recommended one part fluoride per million parts of water.

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:46.170
The people of Grand Rapids pay only $0.07 per person a year for fluoridation.

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.970
All Grand Rapids children benefitted.

00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:54.040
The youngsters, as you can see, have less than half as many bad baby teeth.

00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:59.280
The 13-year-olds have fewer bad teeth, four compared to ten.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:03.360
The older children also have much less tooth decay,

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:07.620
especially if they started drinking the water in their first month or so.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:16.740
Evanston, Illinois found controlled fluoridation as effective as Grand Rapids.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:24.820
Before fluoridation, only about one percent of the 12-year-olds in Evanston had perfect teeth like these.

00:08:24.820 --> 00:08:31.100
After eleven years of fluoridation, thirteen times as many 12-year-olds had perfect teeth.

00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:34.000
None missing, decayed, or filled.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:38.640
Eleven years of fluoridation in Evanston cost $88,000,

00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:45.220
but Evanston parents saved almost one-quarter of a million dollars in the cost of dental care

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:48.180
and improved the health of their children.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:53.700
The experience of a town like Aurora, Illinois with natural fluoridation

00:08:53.700 --> 00:08:56.740
shows how fluoridation lasts a lifetime.

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:07.800
In Aurora, seven times as many adults have all their teeth than do adults in a non-fluoride city nearby.

00:09:09.100 --> 00:09:13.000
You may have heard that fluoridation causes unsightly teeth.

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:18.160
In Grand Rapids, a half of one percent of the 12- to 16-year-olds

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:23.300
have what dentists call mild fluorosis, like Marion.

00:09:24.780 --> 00:09:27.660
But the general effect is good here.

00:09:27.660 --> 00:09:28.840
Here's a better view.

00:09:28.840 --> 00:09:33.100
As you can see, locating fluorosis is a job for a specialist.

00:09:33.100 --> 00:09:36.820
There it is, those opaque white spots.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:42.840
Opponents say fluoridation makes teeth ugly, but I wouldn't call those teeth ugly.

00:09:43.460 --> 00:09:48.600
Some people object that fluoridation takes away their individual freedom and rights.

00:09:48.600 --> 00:09:54.220
But if that's true, then chlorine and other water treatment chemicals take away these rights.

00:09:54.220 --> 00:09:58.880
Have older people any reason to be concerned about fluoridation?

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:00.520
Certainly not.

00:10:01.040 --> 00:10:08.420
In the specific case of heart difficulties, Dr. Paul Dudley White, the noted heart specialist, says,

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:15.860
"Elderly people with tired hearts need have no fear of fluoridated water. It is safe for all."

00:10:16.360 --> 00:10:20.220
We can say the same of any malady of an older person.

00:10:20.220 --> 00:10:24.960
Fluoride has no adverse effect on any of the internal organs.

00:10:24.960 --> 00:10:29.840
Not on kidneys, liver, stomach, heart, or any other.

00:10:30.220 --> 00:10:37.320
All people of all ages, sick or well, can drink fluoridated water without question, doubt, or hesitation.

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:43.400
I think older people should consider fluoridation a wonderful gift to the young ones they love.

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:48.980
That's why many older people work so hard to bring about fluoridation programs.

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:53.180
It means better health for their grandchildren and doesn't harm a living soul.

00:10:53.860 --> 00:10:58.140
Some people point out that a certain amount of fluoride is wasted.

00:10:58.140 --> 00:10:59.860
There's some waste, of course.

00:10:59.860 --> 00:11:02.120
All the water is not drunk.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:06.500
In that respect, it's no different from other water treatment chemicals.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:16.240
But since $1.00 invested for fluoridation eventually saves $56.00 in dental care, I'd scarcely call it wasteful.

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:22.540
Other people urge that children take fluoride tablets instead of fluoridating the water supply.

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:29.740
Well, as a pediatrician I simply can't recommend a tablet a child must take every day for eight or ten years.

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:35.620
Tooth-brushing, of course, is still important for oral hygiene,

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:38.960
but toothpaste can never be a substitute for fluoridation.

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:41.660
But I'm getting away from the really important things.

00:11:41.660 --> 00:11:46.380
Here they are, just three key points to remember about fluoridation.

00:11:46.380 --> 00:11:51.480
It has never been known to harm anyone, old or young, ill or well.

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:59.680
It prevents two out of every three cavities, and it costs about a dime a year a person.

00:11:59.680 --> 00:12:02.840
We're not really talking about a theory.

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:07.060
We're not primarily concerned with the process called fluoridation.

00:12:07.060 --> 00:12:11.340
We're interested in flesh and blood children, healthy, happy children.

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:15.100
Here's Linda and Carol and Lynn.

00:12:15.100 --> 00:12:17.860
And the twins, Jan and Jean.

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:21.620
Here in Cleveland, we protect their teeth with fluoridated water.

00:12:21.620 --> 00:12:24.480
We started back in 1956.

00:12:24.480 --> 00:12:27.780
All I can say is, I hope you fluoridate.

00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:29.620
I know you'll be glad you did.

00:12:29.620 --> 00:12:47.520
[Music]

